Z||000000||Uaana||07-27-2000||03:34 PM||||O.K.  I'll take any decent anwser..<BR>The question is Will 1st Gen MR2 seats fit in our cars? Size wise I'm pretty sure they are dead on.. But the mounting brackets are completely different.<BR>Ideas?<P>In case you are wondering I found a perfect set of black leather seats with all the non power goodies that should be on ours. like adj lumbar, adj side bolster oh and leather!<BR>Thanks in advance.||||reg||3
Z||000001||GT Bastard||07-27-2000||04:39 PM||||I'm fairly certain that they are not a direct bolt-in, however....  It wouldn't be difficult to have someone fabricate new mounting brackets or an adaptor plate.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||07-27-2000||04:47 PM||||The MR2 brackets are probably spot welded to the floor pan. Drill out those spot welds in the floor pan of the MR2 and remove the brackets. Take the brackets out of the MR2 and weld them to your fiero's floor pan. You can then mount the MR2 seats in your fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000003||sloGT||07-27-2000||05:31 PM||||well I can tell you that they are not spot welded but only bolted in,after I totaled my 87 mr2 (I know,I know rice),I mounted the seats in my nissan truck.dont know how to go about the fiero but hhmmmmm.might have to yank the seats out and try. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||07-27-2000||08:39 PM||||That makes it easier then. All you have to do is drill out the fiero mounts and weld in the MR2 mounts. I did this to an Impala once and it worked great.||||reg||1
